/textbook/build/quiz-widget-612a97c1bdda77747487ee7393cbf45b.mjs","model":{"question":"A z-test for μ with alternative Hₐ: μ < μ₀ produces z = −1.5. Which expression gives the p-value?","choices":[{"correct":true,"text":"P(Z ≤ −1.5)","feedback":"Correct! For a left-tailed test, the p-value is the area to the left of the observed test statistic: P(Z ≤ −1.5) ≈ 0.067."},{"correct":false,"text":"P(Z ≥ −1.5)","feedback":"The area to the right of −1.5 (≈ 0.933) would essentially measure agreement with H₀."},{"correct":false,"text":"2P(Z ≤ −1.5)","feedback":"Doubling is only for two-sided alternatives."}],"multi":false,"hint":"A \"less than\" alternative is left-tailed.","explanation":""},"key":"wb3KAr003K"},{"type":"anywidget","esm":"/textbook/build/quiz-widget-612a97c1bdda77747487ee7393cbf45b.mjs","model":{"question":"In example 2, the p-value was 0.012. Which is the correct interpretation?","choices":[{"correct":true,"text":"If μ were 250 ppm, the probability of a sample mean as far from 250 as 247 is (in either direction) would be 0.012","feedback":"Correct! If the mean concentration really were 250 ppm, there would be only a 0.012 probability of getting a sample mean at least 2.5 standard deviations away from 250 (in either direction)."},{"correct":false,"text":"There is a 1.2% chance that the mean concentration is 250 ppm","feedback":"The p-value is not the probability that H₀ is true."},{"correct":false,"text":"If μ were 250 ppm, the probability of a sample mean of 247 or lower would be 0.012","feedback":"Since the alternative is two-sided, \"as extreme\" includes both directions, not just below."}],"multi":false,"hint":"Condition on H₀ (μ = 250) being true, and remember the two-sided alternative.","explanation":""},"key":"bhdMyhmhnn"}],"key":"oxTTJC6gY7"}],"key":"XedCCnZv94"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Stating Hypotheses and Summarizing Data for a Mean","url":"/pages/m15-hypothesis-testing-for-the-populatio